{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_pilot_17\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_30bad96e288a61c8\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_30bad96e288a61c8/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Audio playback scrubber/clock freeze\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-17T00:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\", \"member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that sound stops and the display stays at 0:00 after dragging the waveform back to the start on AUD-741 in Firefox 132.0.2; reopening restores playback until seeking again.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that reloading permits one listen, but moving the scrubber changes the play triangle while the clock never advances on AUD-754 in Chrome 131.0.6778.85.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9107\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks for the task ID and browser build in the AUD-741 thread and says a second reproduction is needed before filing.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9104\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports reproducing the stuck clock on AUD-754 and reports that the downloaded WAV plays normally.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9104\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current audio incident triage guideline directs collecting task IDs, browser versions and reproduction steps for a reproducible player freeze after seeking, then sending one scoped engineering incident for the affected player reports. Verbatim quote: \\\"For a reproducible player freeze after seeking, collect task IDs, browser versions, and reproduction steps. Send one scoped engineering incident for the affected player reports.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:pilot-audio-incident-triage@1.3:3b2b70f0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current media-input quality FAQ calls for preserving the sample and using the media-input quality flag when a local copy is confirmed silent and the player advances normally; missing task IDs or local playback checks must be requested before assigning a disposition.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:pilot-media-input-quality-faq@1.1:00309a9c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors report that the player clock stops advancing after seeking, with reopening or reloading restoring playback only temporarily.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9107\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports reproducing the stuck clock on one task; current guidance calls for one scoped engineering incident for reproducible player freezes after seeking.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"k:pilot-audio-incident-triage@1.3:3b2b70f0\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9104\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that dragging the waveform back to the start stops sound and leaves the display at 0:00 on AUD-741 in Firefox 132.0.2.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that moving the scrubber changes the play triangle without advancing the clock on AUD-754 in Chrome 131.0.6778.85.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9107\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the AUD-741 thread, a QA tutor asked for the task ID and browser build and said a second reproduction was needed before filing; the tutor supplied the ID and full browser version.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9104\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U9106\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the AUD-754 thread, a QA tutor also reports that the downloaded WAV plays normally.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U9104\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Report a technical issue to engineering. Instruction: Send engineering one scoped incident covering both reported player freezes, including the task IDs, browser versions and reported reproduction steps. Draft to copy: Please investigate a player freeze after seeking on two tasks. Two tutors report that the clock stops advancing after seeking and that reopening or reloading restores playback only temporarily.\\n- AUD-741, Firefox 132.0.2: a tutor reports that dragging the waveform back to the start stops sound and leaves the display at 0:00; reopening restores playback until seeking again.\\n- AUD-754, Chrome 131.0.6778.85: a tutor reports that moving the scrubber changes the play triangle but the clock never advances; reloading permits one listen.\\nA QA tutor reports reproducing the stuck clock on AUD-754 and says its downloaded WAV plays normally. Scope: Limit the incident to the reported player failures on AUD-741 and AUD-754; the reports do not establish a technical cause.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"k:pilot-audio-incident-triage@1.3:3b2b70f0\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current triage guideline calls for one engineering incident for reproducible freezes after seeking, and the reports provide the required details.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"k:pilot-audio-incident-triage@1.3:3b2b70f0\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"k:pilot-media-input-quality-faq@1.1:00309a9c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Two tutors report player-clock failures after seeking on separate tasks, and a QA tutor reports reproducing one failure, warranting a scoped technical report now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac is UNRESOLVED: The tutor supplies the requested task and browser details but reports that seeking triggers the failure again after reopening; the thread establishes no lasting resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports failure after moving the scrubber, and a QA tutor reports reproducing it; neither message establishes a fix or restored player operation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity HIGH: Two tutors report comparable seeking failures on separate tasks in the same batch and morning, suggesting disruption beyond one isolated task despite temporary recovery.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\\\": Two distinct tutors report that seeking stops the player clock on AUD-741 and AUD-754, with reopening or reloading restoring playback only temporarily.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U9106\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U9106 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U9107\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U9107 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\", \"thread_id\": \"1792137900.000000\", \"author_id\": \"U9106\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T08:05:00Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U9106\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The sound stops when I drag the waveform back to the start, and the time display sits at 0:00. Task AUD-741, Firefox 132. It played the first time.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138020.000000\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\", \"thread_id\": \"1792137900.000000\", \"author_id\": \"U9104\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T08:07:00Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U9106\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can you send the task ID and browser build? We need a second reproduction before filing.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b097379f48ad7a130b9adbac\", \"thread_id\": \"1792137900.000000\", \"author_id\": \"U9106\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T08:09:00Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U9106\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"AUD-741, Firefox 132.0.2. Reopening restores it until I seek again.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164\", \"thread_id\": \"1792139520.000000\", \"author_id\": \"U9107\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T08:32:00Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U9107\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Reloading gives me one listen. As soon as I move the scrubber, the play triangle changes but the clock never advances. AUD-754, Chrome 131.0.6778.85.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_77774044871dcbe2f1dfe164\", \"thread_id\": \"1792139520.000000\", \"author_id\": \"U9104\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T08:34:00Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U9107\", \"thread_starter_role